msgid "Write logs from a managed workflow, report errors that your local notebook can read, and save partial work when a job is canceled."
msgstr "Zapisuj logi z zarządzanego przepływu pracy, zgłaszaj błędy, które może odczytać lokalny notatnik, i zapisuj częściową pracę, gdy zadanie zostanie anulowane."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs and handle errors"
msgstr "Zapisuj logi i obsługuj błędy"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore levelname */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs and handle errors {#write-logs-and-handle-errors}"
msgstr "Zapisuj logi i obsługuj błędy {#write-logs-and-handle-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* <Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Placeholder content\">\n"
"- **Errors from custom workflows.** A managed workflow stores a structured error for a custom workflow only when the workflow calls `send_error()`. If custom workflows get the same top-level handler as Catalog Functions, remove the handler from [Best practice: report errors with send_error()](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error).\n"
"- **Time after cancel.** Confirm how long a job can run after `SIGTERM` before the managed workflow stops it.\n"
